The need for a clearly defined and consistent '''invasion biology terminology''' has been acknowledged by many sources. ''[[Invasive species]]'', or ''invasive [[Introduced species|exotics]]'', is a nomenclature term and categorization phrase used for flora and fauna, and for specific restoration-preservation processes in native [[habitat]]s. ''Invasion biology'' is the study of these organisms and the processes of species invasion. 

The terminology in this article contains definitions for invasion biology terms in common usage today, taken from accessible publications.  References for each definition are included.  Terminology relates primarily to invasion biology terms with some [[ecology]] terms included to clarify language and phrases on linked articles.

