'''Dr. A.P.J. Abdul Kalam Technical University''' ('''AKTU'''), before 2015 known as the '''Uttar Pradesh Technical University''' ('''UPTU'''), is a public [[collegiate university]] in [[Lucknow|Lucknow, Uttar Pradesh]], India. It was established as the Uttar Pradesh Technical University through the [[Government of Uttar Pradesh]] on 8 May 2000. To reduce workload and to ensure proper management, the university was bifurcated into separate universities, Gautam Buddh Technical University (GBTU) and Mahamaya Technical University (MTU), with effect from 1 May 2010.<ref name="circular">{{cite web|title=UPTU Circular|url=http://uptu.ac.in/colleges/clogin_28052010.pdf|access-date=25 March 2011|location=[[Lucknow]]|page=1|language=hi|date=28 May 2010|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110721151149/http://uptu.ac.in/colleges/clogin_28052010.pdf|archive-date=21 July 2011|df=dmy-all}}</ref> In 2013, as a new government came into power, the university was formed again by combining the two on 5 January 2013.<ref>{{cite news | url=http://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/home/education/news/Govt-merges-MTU-GBTU-to-form-UPTU/articleshow/17908059.cms | work=The Times Of India | title=Govt merges MTU, GBTU to form UPTU | access-date=11 March 2014 | archive-date=7 December 2014 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20141207084643/http://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/home/education/news/Govt-merges-MTU-GBTU-to-form-UPTU/articleshow/17908059.cms | url-status=live }}</ref>

It is an affiliating university, with approximately 800 colleges affiliated to it.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.uptu.ac.in/academics/inst_list.asp |title=Institute List |publisher=Gautam Buddh Technical University |access-date=25 April 2012 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120421123135/http://www.uptu.ac.in/academics/inst_list.asp |archive-date=21 April 2012 |df=dmy }}</ref> The university was earlier on the [[IET Lucknow]] campus.  Now it is in its newly inaugurated campus in Jankipuram, Lucknow. Additionally, the university had a Centre and Regional Office in [[Noida|Noida, Uttar Pradesh]].<ref name=":1" />

